            "scope_concern": "Optional Host-set bound on the permits one source holds at once on the proven lane (cause `source_pending_permits`; disabled when not set, no default; slot freed by the atomic outcome of either kind, once, also after a key rotation); one effective value per budget group across the workers sharing one Redis, `off` included, checked by the store before any reservation and changed only by an explicit rebind; an exception to the package constants (DEC-028, now DEC-035) that leaves their other values unchanged",
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "title": "Optional Proven-Lane Pending-Permit Limit and Shared Admission Configuration"
        },
        {
            "canonical_contract_owner": "CallerTimeMilliseconds`, `CallerTimeDecimalMilliseconds*StoreInterface`, `CallerTimeStore`, `RedisFullCapabilityStore`, `docs/guides/USAGE_GUIDE.md",
            "decision_id": "[DEC-039](DEC-039_DECIMAL_MILLISECOND_CALLER_TIME_CAPABILITIES.md)",
            "decision_record": "docs/decisions/DEC-039_DECIMAL_MILLISECOND_CALLER_TIME_CAPABILITIES.md",
            "record_exists": true,
            "scope_concern": "Additive optional store interfaces that receive the caller's epoch time in milliseconds as a canonical decimal string (0 to 2^53 − 1) where a native integer cannot hold it (32-bit PHP); the runtime prefers them, calls a native-integer-only caller-time store when the value fits and raises `RateLimiterException` before the call when it does not, and leaves a store with its own clock unchanged; no existing interface or signature changes. Owner-approved on #215 (2026-11-14).",
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "title": "Decimal-Millisecond Caller-Time Store Capabilities"
        },
        {
            "canonical_contract_owner": "RedisFullCapabilityStore`, `RedisRequestOverlay`, `RATE_LIMITER_PACKAGE_REFERENCE.md",
            "decision_id": "[DEC-040](DEC-040_LEGACY_LIFECYCLE_READ_EXPIRY_BEYOND_THE_EXACT_REPRESENTATION_RANGE.md)",
            "decision_record": "docs/decisions/DEC-040_LEGACY_LIFECYCLE_READ_EXPIRY_BEYOND_THE_EXACT_REPRESENTATION_RANGE.md",
            "record_exists": true,
            "scope_concern": "The Redis lifecycle read of a legacy score (no generation, no stored `expiresAt`): the expiry `ceil((callerNowMs + remainingPTTL) / 1000)` is exact on the split branch (a PTTL the script sees of at most `2^53 − 1` ms, valid caller clock, lifetime captured without loss; `2^53 − 1` is the bound of the exact calculation, not a rejection limit); above that bound the original arithmetic remains even for a representable PTTL, and in the request overlay when the absolute expiry cannot be held exactly, outside the proven-exact conditions the existing replies or failures are preserved (an inexact expiry, or the existing validation refusal); no cap, no new refusal, no change to the DTO, the clock or the overlay. Owner-approved on #250 (2026-11-16).",
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "title": "Legacy Lifecycle Read Expiry Beyond the Exact Representation Range"
        },
        {
            "canonical_contract_owner": "Approved, not yet accepted as implemented; intended owners: the ownership coordinator, the runtime entries, `RedisFullCapabilityStore`, `RequestAtomicStoreInterface` (one nested-call sentence); design `investigations/fiber-request-ownership-260/EXCLUSIVITY_DESIGN.md",
            "decision_id": "[DEC-041](DEC-041_EXCLUSIVE_REQUEST_OWNERSHIP_AND_EXPLICIT_OVERLAP_REFUSAL.md)",
            "decision_record": "docs/decisions/DEC-041_EXCLUSIVE_REQUEST_OWNERSHIP_AND_EXPLICIT_OVERLAP_REFUSAL.md",
            "record_exists": true,
            "scope_concern": "Principle B and the design contract M1–M7: a runtime graph and the store objects it is built on serve one independent call at a time; an independent call that begins while another is in flight, on the same graph or on a resource shared with another graph, is refused explicitly (`OverlappingRequestException`) before it can alter, consume or observe the state of the call in flight; ownership by resource identity, all-or-none two-phase acquisition, execution-context identity with Host-crossing markers, optional context provider with per-resource domain binding and provider leases; every public entry and direct capability guarded; readers refused; legitimate nesting preserved; independent graphs and Redis conflicts (DEC-037) unchanged. **Approved, not yet accepted as implemented**: the code at `main@316b1de9` does not enforce it; the implementation under review on PR #266 is unaccepted (#260 stays open). Owner-approved on #260 (principle 2026-11-18; M1–M7 2026-11-18).",
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "title": "Exclusive Request Ownership and Explicit Refusal of an Overlapping Call"
        }
    ],
